{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWKi1Ksvr7As7qgUrsjN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GHJYuFhmH4UeaWxHT7rvQX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/analysis/IMPACT_REPORT.md","content":"# Dependency Graph Impact Report: tokio → hyper → tonic\n\nRepos analyzed (pinned checkouts):\n- `/workspace/tokio` — tag `tokio-1.0.0` (crate `tokio` v1.0.0)\n- `/workspace/hyper` — tag `v0.14.0` (crate `hyper` v0.14.0)\n- `/workspace/tonic` — tag `v0.6.0` (crate `tonic` v0.6.0)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Dependency chain with exact version constraints\n\n```\ntonic v0.6.0  (/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml)\n ├─ hyper = \"0.14.4\"            (features = [\"full\"], optional, gated by \"transport\")\n ├─ h2 = \"0.3\"                  (optional, gated by \"transport\")\n ├─ tokio = \"1.0.1\"             (features = [\"net\"], optional, gated by \"transport\";\n │                                also pulls in \"tokio/macros\", \"tokio/time\" via the\n │                                \"transport\" feature union at line 40-41)\n ├─ tokio-util = \"0.6\"          (features = [\"codec\"])\n ├─ tokio-stream = \"0.1\"\n └─ tower = \"0.4.7\"             (features = [\"balance\",\"buffer\",\"discover\",\"limit\",\n                                   \"load\",\"make\",\"timeout\",\"util\"], optional)\n\nhyper v0.14.0  (/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml)\n ├─ tokio = \"1\"                 (features = [\"sync\"])   [runtime deps add: fs, macros,\n │                                io-std, io-util, rt, rt-multi-thread, sync, time,\n │                                test-util — dev-only]\n ├─ h2 = \"0.3\"                  (optional, enabled by feature \"http2\")\n ├─ tower-service = \"0.3\"\n └─ tokio-util = \"0.6\"          (dev-dependency only, features = [\"codec\"])\n\ntokio v1.0.0  (/workspace/tokio/tokio/Cargo.toml)\n ├─ mio = \"0.7.6\"               (optional; backs the \"net\" feature)\n ├─ bytes = \"1.0.0\"             (optional; backs \"io-util\")\n ├─ parking_lot = \"0.11.0\"      (optional)\n ├─ num_cpus = \"1.8.0\"          (optional; backs \"rt-multi-thread\")\n └─ tokio-util = \"0.6.0\"        (sibling workspace crate, /workspace/tokio/tokio-util/Cargo.toml)\n```\n\nChain: `tonic v0.6.0` → requires `hyper ^0.14.4` and `tokio ^1.0.1` (both directly, for\nthe `transport` feature) → `hyper v0.14.0` → requires `tokio ^1`.\n\ntonic therefore has **two independent edges into tokio**: a direct one (`tonic/Cargo.toml`\nline 76) and a transitive one through hyper (`hyper/Cargo.toml` line 36). Both must\nresolve to a single `tokio` version in the final dependency graph (Cargo unifies by\nsemver-compatible range), so the tightest constraint wins — here that is tonic's own\n`tokio = \"1.0.1\"`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. tokio APIs that hyper uses which tonic depends on transitively\n\nhyper's public surface embeds tokio types directly, so any consumer that touches that\nsurface (tonic) inherits a dependency on those tokio APIs even without importing tokio\nitself in that call path.\n\n| tokio API | Used in hyper at | Exposed to tonic via |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite, ReadBuf}` | `/workspace/hyper/src/server/tcp.rs` (AddrStream impls, lines 265-284), `/workspace/hyper/src/client/conn.rs`, `/workspace/hyper/src/server/conn.rs`, `/workspace/hyper/src/proto/h1/io.rs`, `/workspace/hyper/src/proto/h2/{client,server}.rs`, `/workspace/hyper/src/upgrade.rs` | `hyper::server::conn::AddrStream` (re-exported `/workspace/hyper/src/server/conn.rs:80`) is named directly in `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/conn.rs:1`; tonic's own `Connected`/IO wrapper types (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/service/io.rs:6`, `.../service/tls.rs:9`, `.../channel/mod.rs:27-28`) implement the *same* `AsyncRead`/`AsyncWrite` traits, so a signature change (e.g. to `poll_read`/`ReadBuf`) breaks hyper's `AddrStream` and tonic's IO shims simultaneously |\n| `tokio::net::{TcpListener, TcpStream}` | `/workspace/hyper/src/server/tcp.rs:6,227` (backs `AddrIncoming`/`AddrStream`) | tonic accepts connections through `hyper::Server::builder(incoming)` (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/mod.rs:498`), so its accept loop is driven by hyper's `TcpListener`-backed `AddrIncoming` |\n| `tokio::task::spawn` / `tokio::task::JoinHandle` | `/workspace/hyper/src/common/exec.rs:48` (default `Exec::execute` — used whenever no custom executor is supplied), `/workspace/hyper/src/client/connect/dns.rs:32` | tonic's default server (`Server::serve`, `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/mod.rs`) relies on hyper's default `Exec::Default` to drive each connection future via `tokio::spawn`; a change to spawn's `Send`/lifetime requirements affects tonic's service futures without tonic calling `tokio::spawn` itself in that path |\n| `tokio::time::{Sleep, Interval, Instant, sleep, interval}` | `/workspace/hyper/src/proto/h2/ping.rs:36,63` (HTTP/2 keep-alive ping timer), `/workspace/hyper/src/client/pool.rs:11,418` (idle connection pool eviction) | tonic exposes `http2_keepalive_interval`/`http2_keepalive_timeout` config (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/mod.rs`, `.../channel/endpoint.rs`) that is implemented entirely by hyper's `tokio::time::Sleep`-based ping timer — a `Sleep`/`Interval` polling change ripples into tonic's keepalive behavior with no tonic-side code change |\n| `tokio::sync::oneshot` | `/workspace/hyper/src/upgrade.rs:16`, `/workspace/hyper/src/server/mod.rs:181` (graceful shutdown signal) | tonic's `Server::serve_with_shutdown` forwards its shutdown future into hyper's graceful-shutdown machinery, which is built on this `oneshot` channel |\n\ntonic also uses several tokio APIs **directly** (not just transitively), which doubles\nthe blast radius of a tokio change on tonic:\n- `tokio::io::{AsyncRead, AsyncWrite, ReadBuf}` — `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/service/io.rs:6`, `.../service/tls.rs:9`, `.../server/mod.rs:51`, `.../channel/mod.rs:28`\n- `tokio::net::TcpStream` — `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/conn.rs:3`\n- `tokio::io::DuplexStream` (`impl Connected for tokio::io::DuplexStream`) — `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/conn.rs:101`\n- `tokio::spawn` / `tokio::task::JoinHandle` — `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/incoming.rs:56,87` (TLS accept loop)\n- `tokio::sync::mpsc::Receiver` — `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/service/discover.rs:10`\n- `tokio::time::Sleep` / `tokio::time::sleep` — `/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/service/grpc_timeout.rs:12,63`\n\nSo a tokio bump that touches `io` (AsyncRead/AsyncWrite/ReadBuf), `net`, `time::Sleep`,\n`sync::{oneshot,mpsc}`, or `task::spawn` must be validated against **both** hyper's\ninternal implementation and tonic's own transport code — the same trait/type is\nimplemented or consumed independently in three places.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Version pinning conflicts found across the three repos\n\nTwo concrete conflicts exist between the constraints declared in `tonic`'s manifest and\nthe actual pinned versions of `hyper` and `tokio` checked out in this workspace:\n\n1. **tokio under-satisfied**\n   `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:76` declares `tokio = { version = \"1.0.1\", features = [\"net\"], optional = true }`\n   (Cargo caret range `>=1.0.1, <2.0.0`), but `/workspace/tokio/tokio/Cargo.toml:11` pins\n   `version = \"1.0.0\"`. `1.0.0` does **not** satisfy `>=1.0.1`, so building tonic's\n   `transport` feature against this exact tokio checkout fails dependency resolution.\n\n2. **hyper under-satisfied**\n   `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:74` declares `hyper = { version = \"0.14.4\", features = [\"full\"], optional = true }`\n   (range `>=0.14.4, <0.15.0`), but `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:3` pins `version = \"0.14.0\"`.\n   `0.14.0` does not satisfy `>=0.14.4`, so tonic's `transport` feature also cannot\n   resolve against this exact hyper checkout.\n\nEverything else in the graph is internally consistent:\n- `h2 = \"0.3\"` in both `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:73` and `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:31` — compatible.\n- `tokio-util = \"0.6\"` in `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:61`, `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:64` (dev-dep), and the actual crate version `0.6.0` at `/workspace/tokio/tokio-util/Cargo.toml:10` — compatible.\n- `http = \"0.2\"` and `http-body = \"0.4\"/\"0.4.4\"` are aligned between `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:27-28` and `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:54,58` — compatible.\n- `tower-service = \"0.3\"` matches in both `/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:35` and `/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:63`.\n\nThe first conflict (tokio `1.0.0` vs. required `1.0.1`) is the one that actually matters\nfor \"a tokio version bump cascading through hyper into tonic\": tonic's `transport`\nfeature was written against a slightly newer tokio patch than what's pinned here, so\neven *before* any intentional bump, this workspace's exact-pinned combination does not\nbuild tonic's transport layer as-is.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Upgrade coordination strategy\n\nBecause tonic depends on tokio both directly and transitively (through hyper), and\nduplicates several of hyper's tokio-facing trait implementations, a safe bump has to\nmove through the stack in dependency order and re-validate each shared boundary:\n\n1. **Bump tokio first, in isolation.** Update `/workspace/tokio` and run its own test\n   suite, paying special attention to `tokio/src/io/util/mem.rs` (`DuplexStream`),\n   `tokio/src/net/*` (`TcpListener`/`TcpStream`), `tokio/src/time/*` (`Sleep`/`Interval`),\n   and `tokio/src/sync/*` (`oneshot`, `mpsc`, `Semaphore`) — these are exactly the\n   modules both hyper and tonic implement traits against or consume types from.\n   Confirm the new version still satisfies hyper's `tokio = \"1\"` bound\n   (`/workspace/hyper/Cargo.toml:36`) and tonic's `tokio = \"1.0.1\"` bound\n   (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/Cargo.toml:76`) — resolve conflict #1 above by bumping the\n   pinned