end-to-end).\n\n5. **Keep the three manifests' floors in lockstep going forward**: because tonic pins a\n   *tighter* tokio floor (`1.0.1`) than hyper does (`1`), and a tighter hyper floor\n   (`0.14.4`) than what's checked out here (`0.14.0`), any future tokio/hyper bump should\n   first check whether it *also* requires raising tonic's declared floors — tonic is the\n   most sensitive point in the chain because it duplicates hyper's trait implementations\n   instead of only consuming hyper's public types.\n\n6. **Watch `hyper::server::conn::AddrStream` and `hyper::client::connect::{Connected,\n   Connection}` as the highest-risk rename/removal targets** — tonic imports these\n   concrete hyper types by name (`/workspace/tonic/tonic/src/transport/server/conn.rs:1`,\n   `.../service/io.rs:2`, `.../channel/mod.rs:19`, `.../channel/endpoint.rs:263`,\n   `.../service/discover.rs:36`, `.../service/connection.rs:5-7`). A hyper release that\n   relocates or removes these types (independent of any tokio change) breaks tonic\n   directly and is not caught by tokio-focused testing alone.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
